d source side is the partition induced by the computed flow rather than an independently selected minimum cut."},"unreachable_nodes_are_handled_by_compone":{"score":"yes","reasoning":"Incremental closeness explicitly recognizes nodes unreachable from both modified-edge endpoints as belonging to unaffected components and preserves their previous values; reachable nodes are evaluated from their finite-distance component."},"a_group_measure_treats_the_group_as_one":{"score":"yes","reasoning":"`_group_dependency` sets the avoiding-path count to zero on entry to any group node and computes one through-group fraction per path, treating the set as a single interception unit."},"one_shared_accessor_serves_the_algorithm":{"score":"yes","reasoning":"There is one `_capacity_function` implementation in `flow.utils`, imported by the flow implementations; no separate capacity-resolution copies are introduced in each algorithm."},"a_specifier_given_as_a_name_is_distingui":{"score":"yes","reasoning":"The accessor distinguishes callable values from attribute-name specifiers: callables pass through, while names are converted into edge-attribute lookup functions with infinite capacity as the missing-value default."}}

